{
  "_comment": [
    "Third-party components shipped in Revere's packages, and where each one's licence text comes from.",
    "scripts/licenses/fetch_licenses.py reads this, downloads every licence into licenses/<id>.txt and",
    "writes licenses/README.md. Edit this file, not the generated ones, then re-run the script.",
    "",
    "platforms: win = Windows installer, mac = macOS .app, appimage = Linux AppImage, deb = Raspberry Pi .deb.",
    "sources, tried in order until one works:",
    "  {\"url\": ...}      a licence file, fetched as is (several may be listed with \"all\": true to keep them all)",
    "  {\"debian\": pkg}   Debian's machine-readable copyright file for source package pkg (sources.debian.org),",
    "                      used for distribution libraries and for the many libraries inside the Windows FFmpeg",
    "  {\"repo\": path}    a file already in this repository",
    "  {\"text\": ...}     a short statement written here (public-domain code that has no licence file)"
  ],
